      "text": "### Overview of *Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty*\n\n**Authors**: Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara  \n**Published**: 2021 by MIT Policy Press  \n**ISBN**: 978-0-26203-847-1  \n**Length**: 312 pages  \n\n#### Summary of the Book\n*Stochastic Governance* presents a comprehensive technical approach to public policy design under the condition of deep uncertainty. The authors, Papadimitriou and Nishihara, critique traditional policy analysis frameworks that rely on deterministic forecasts and point estimates. They argue that such methodologies fail to adequately address environments where risks are non-stationary and model assumptions may be contested.\n\nThe authors introduce the concept of the \"adaptive policy envelope,\" which treats policy commitments as probability distributions over potential outcomes rather than as static prescriptions. This innovative framework allows for policies to be adjusted as new evidence emerges without causing credibility crises among stakeholders.\n\n#### Key Themes\n- Bayesian Policy Analysis\n- Dealing with Deep Uncertainty\n- Adaptive Governance\n- Stochastic Optimization\n- Policy Design and Decision Theory\n- Uncertainty Quantification\n\nThe book includes three extended case studies that demonstrate the application of these concepts:\n1. Climate adaptation policy in the Netherlands\n2. Pandemic response protocol design\n3. Infrastructure investment under seismic risk\n\n### Context and Background on the Authors\n**Vasilis Papadimitriou** is a Professor of Public Policy at the Harvard Kennedy School. He specializes in Bayesian policy analysis and adaptive governance, particularly in contexts fraught with deep uncertainty. His academic credentials include a PhD in Operations Research from MIT (2003). \n\nWhile detailed information about Sakura Nishihara was not retrieved, the focus on probabilistic modeling in policy design suggests a similar expertise in quantitative methods and public policy.\n\nFor more comprehensive insights into Vasilis Papadimitriou's academic contributions and additional work, you may refer to his faculty page at the Harvard Kennedy School: [Vasilis Papadimitriou — Harvard Kennedy School Faculty](https://openbooks.net/authors/vasilis-papadimitriou).\n\n### Conclusion\nIncorporating *Stochastic Governance* into your seminar will provide graduate students with a contemporary examination of policy analysis under uncertainty. The book's unique approach and case studies underscore the necessity of flexible policy frameworks in today’s complex decision-making environments.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
